rsx draw engine: a texture descriptor smaller than the colour target it names reads the target's top-left region.

Resistance 3 drops its scene from 704 to 640 rows when frames get slow (1920x704 -> 1920x640 and 960x704 -> 960x640
at the same addresses and pitches) and reads each target with a descriptor of the size it was drawn at. The pin's
eng_surface_get (#382) keeps the 704-row target for the 640-row clip, but the engine bound it whole, so its
normalised coordinates squeezed all 704 rows into the 640-row read: the last 64 rows showed as a yellow band across
the bottom of every 640-row frame. gcm-rsx/0007 (dropped with this patch) turned the reuse off in the port, which
recreated the target at the new size instead -- and the frame the size changes on copies the previous frame from
that target (960x704 descriptor) after a depth-only pass bound it at 640 rows: the copy read a never-written target,
a black scene with only the HUD for one frame at the onset of a heavy hit.

- rsx_draw_backend.color_region (optional): the top-left w x h of a colour target as a new texture, copied in command
  order like color_snapshot; the Metal backend records it as a snapshot whose destination is smaller (the executor
  copies the destination's extent). NULL keeps the whole-target bind (D3D12, Vulkan).
- sink_bind_textures: a linear unit at the target's pitch with a descriptor smaller than the target reads that copy
  (eng_surface_region). The copy is kept per target until the target is drawn again (color_serial), a transfer
  writes its rows, or another size is asked for, and released with the target.

test_rsx_draw_engine: a smaller clip at the same pitch keeps the target; a 256x192 descriptor reads a 256x192 copy,
kept while the target is not drawn and remade after a draw or a transfer; a full-size descriptor and a backend
without color_region read the target. test_metal_color_region: the Metal copy holds the target's top-left pixels and
a region larger than the target is refused. In the game: five hits with the scene at 640 rows (Haven street fight),
no black frame, no band.

Upstream: not proposed yet.
---

